<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#mwamba-bemba-title">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mwamba (Bemba title)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mwamba is the title of one of the senior chiefs of the Bemba of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, who rules a large territory next to that of the Chitimukulu, the paramount. Holders of the Mwamba title were among the most powerful figures in the 19th-century Bemba state and often succeeded to the paramountcy. The death of Mwamba in 1898 opened the way for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-south-africa-company">British South Africa Company</a> rule.</p></div>
